#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096379 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8f8937b-de15-5d4c-aa77-1d45595fc7af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution"}] :question/id #uuid "201a713a-83ca-5e31-9a4f-257795d7eb1b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4690" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=3 \\\\ y+z=2 \\\\ z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(2)=2 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = 2-2 = 0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $z=2$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(2)=3\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx = 3-2 = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 1,$ $y=0,$ and $z = 2.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 1,0,2 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096380 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de05090a-2461-514a-971d-b83c7cea124e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution Given an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cc8ce97a-3bda-506f-b9d2-98ac7524583a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4691" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{3}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-5=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13,$ $x_2=-7,$ and $x_3 = 5.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096381 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries"}] :question/id #uuid "7b44089c-8ca7-57e5-b390-7900647e3884" :question/math-academy-id "e-4692" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n3x_3=3 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \n\tx_3=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(1)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-1=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 1$ and $x_2 = -3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x_1+(-3)-(1) = 0\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} (3 + 1) = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 2,$ $x_2=-3,$ and $x_3 = 1.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 2,-3,1 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de05090a-2461-514a-971d-b83c7cea124e" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Using Back Substitution Given an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28a64c07-1e37-5008-9614-b71485ada7a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,12,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304955} {:answer/id #uuid "18fae80b-6dea-5c12-a1af-d72bc7e5108c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,-12,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304956} {:answer/id #uuid "264949a0-af89-584e-9adf-a8be61d6a1f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-12,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304957} {:answer/id #uuid "48f920e7-68eb-5ca2-8d90-52212ac5ae19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-22,12,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304958} {:answer/id #uuid "467732f5-8683-5df6-8520-cc82d38631c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-22,-12,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "264949a0-af89-584e-9adf-a8be61d6a1f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-12,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304957} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f63b891-747a-5381-97f9-79b498dc5190" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e303c953-d83b-5fd3-b1b2-48ffdf768a6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129459" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+3z=-2 \\\\  & y+4z=0 \\\\  & z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+4(3)=0\\,⟹\\,y=-12.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-12$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-12)+3(3)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-2+12-9=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1$, $y=-12$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨1,-12,3⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd95bf8e-829a-55b9-89e9-a0d8d899ca04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304976} {:answer/id #uuid "4bf3ff45-c8a5-5493-b4a8-f5463a6bd2ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304977} {:answer/id #uuid "2f8a3db6-c440-5bf6-ae84-805d076130e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-30 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304978} {:answer/id #uuid "be25d5a3-63a1-589a-8d12-f5b0c73b490f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304979} {:answer/id #uuid "72f8e646-aefa-573f-bb99-790398bb6c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd95bf8e-829a-55b9-89e9-a0d8d899ca04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304976} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bdbcdf0-b3ed-5eda-9596-47f9c1d7f98d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304975}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c43eaff-6e8a-54f3-9041-509e363b9890" :question/math-academy-id "q-129615" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\  & -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=7 \\\\  & 2{x}_{3}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n2{x}_{3}=4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{3}=2.\n$$\n\n Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}+3(2)=7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=6-7=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+5(-1)+(2)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-1+5-2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is \n${x}_{1}=2$, ${x}_{2}=-1$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304995 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b02f1c1-08b2-510e-8e1f-64f312f89d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,4,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304997} {:answer/id #uuid "37fabebe-4aac-5c89-aa6c-173d855f3d37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304998} {:answer/id #uuid "499125a6-45eb-51c6-a59d-4a00033ac533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304999} {:answer/id #uuid "1d616cc2-cfac-5774-a7cc-cab8e41e4940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-4,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305000} {:answer/id #uuid "0b6f5e3b-de33-5b71-aefa-ddead7c1603a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,3,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37fabebe-4aac-5c89-aa6c-173d855f3d37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304998} :answer-field/id #uuid "614a3b60-e86f-5567-923f-e609ab89f646" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3ee944c9-4b43-5da0-ab41-c5200c36245b" :question/math-academy-id "q-72980" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+y-z=2 \\\\  & y+3z=6 \\\\  & -z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that\n\n$$\n-z=-3\\,⟹\\,z=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(3)=6\\,⟹\\,y=6-9=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-3$ into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n2x+(-3)-(3)=2\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}(2+3+3)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4$, $y=-3$ and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨4,-3,3⟩.$"}]}
